      "quote": "No amount of 'tonality' or 'framing' or 'case studies' will fix it if your offer is fundamentally positioned as a commodity.",
      "context": "Sales technique can't overcome structural positioning problems. The offer itself must be decommoditized first.",
      "tweetability_score": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "People will always pay more for a thing they can visualize, understand, and compare nothing else to.",
      "context": "Tangibility and uniqueness eliminate price shopping. Abstract services invite comparison.",
      "tweetability_score": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "You think you're unique because you have a 'proprietary system.' But here's what your prospect sees: 'X meetings per month.' 'We'll run ads to your funnel.' They've heard this exact pitch from five other people this week.",
      "context": "Internal differentiation (your POV) means nothing if external perception (their experience) is identical.",
      "tweetability_score": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "When they're buying a service, they're buying your time. When they're buying a product, they're buying a specific outcome delivered through a specific mechanism.",
      "context": "The service vs. product distinction determines whether you compete on price or uniqueness.",
      "tweetability_score": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "The second you're defending your price, you've lost.",
      "context": "Price defense means they've already commoditized you. The goal is to make price defense unnecessary.",
      "tweetability_score": 9
    }
  ],

  "transformation_arcs": [
    {
      "before_state": "Sales calls turn into job interviews where prospects interrogate you about process, tools, timeline, and price. You're being auditioned, not selling.",
      "after_state": "Sales calls become product explanations where prospects ask 'Tell me more about the System' and 'When can we start?' You control the frame.",
      "mechanism": "Product-ization Framework: Name it, scope it, clarify mechanism, create tangible deliverables, anchor outcome, set fixed timeline.",
      "example": "Before: 'We do Facebook ads.' After: 'We built the 90-Day Client Acquisition System for B2B coaches. You get one funnel, 10 ad scripts, and automated follow-ups over 90 days to generate 5-10 booked calls per week without hiring a sales team.'"
    },
    {
      "before_state": "Prospects ghost after hearing your price because they're comparing you to 5 other 'Facebook ads people' who seem cheaper.",
      "after_state": "Prospects can't comparison shop because no one else offers 'your thing.' Price becomes secondary to mechanism fit.",
      "mechanism": "Create a named product with defined scope and tangible deliverables that exists nowhere else in the market.",
      "example": "Instead of competing with all agencies on 'ad management' pricing, you sell 'The Plug-and-Profit Sales Machine' with specific deliverables no one else packages the same way."
    },
    {
      "before_state": "You rely on beating competition to market or being perceived as cheaper to win deals—basically playing roulette.",
      "after_state": "You win based on unique mechanism and defined outcome. Competition becomes irrelevant because you're in a category of one.",
      "mechanism": "Shift from selling time/service to selling a specific outcome through a specific mechanism with specific deliverables.",
      "example": "Agency owners stop competing on 'lead gen service' and start selling 'The 30-Day Sprint Blueprint' with fixed deliverables and timeline."
    }
  ],

