      "why_it_matters": "When you're being interviewed instead of selling, you've been mentally categorized as a commodity vendor, making the close nearly impossible"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Prospects ghost immediately after hearing your price",
      "who_feels_it": "Anyone selling 'premium' services who still gets price-shopped",
      "why_it_matters": "No amount of case studies or positioning fixes this if the market perceives your offer as interchangeable with competitors"
    },
    {
      "problem": "You have to compete by being first to market or cheapest—no other levers to pull",
      "who_feels_it": "Service providers stuck in commoditized markets where speed and price are the only differentiators",
      "why_it_matters": "This isn't a sustainable business model—you're playing roulette, not building equity"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Your 'proprietary system' and expertise don't translate into higher prices or easier closes",
      "who_feels_it": "Experts who've built frameworks but still face price resistance",
      "why_it_matters": "Internal differentiation (what you know) doesn't matter if external perception (what they see) is identical to competitors"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Prospects can't visualize what they're buying, so they default to comparing your hourly rate or retainer to others",
      "who_feels_it": "Service businesses that sell outcomes but package them as ongoing retainers or hourly work",
      "why_it_matters": "Without tangible deliverables, prospects have nothing concrete to evaluate except price"
    },
    {
      "problem": "You're stuck explaining your process over and over, but it never seems to help close the deal",
      "who_feels_it": "Consultants and agencies who lead with methodology instead of product",
      "why_it_matters": "When your mechanism is too complex or vague, prospects can't understand why you're different, so price becomes the tiebreaker"
    },
    {
