      "who_feels_it": "Service providers who've tried niching, case studies, and better copy but still face price resistance",
      "why_it_matters": "Positioning tactics fail if the fundamental offer structure is commoditized—you need structural change, not better marketing"
    }
  ],

  "key_examples_case_studies": [
    {
      "example": "B2B Coach Agency: '90-Day Client Acquisition System'",
      "specifics": "One funnel, 10 ad scripts, automated follow-ups over 90 days to generate 5-10 booked calls per week without hiring a sales team. Mechanism: Turn best content into one offer and run ads to booking page.",
      "lesson": "Specific deliverables (10 scripts, 1 funnel), specific outcome (5-10 calls/week), specific timeline (90 days) makes the offer impossible to compare to generic 'ad management' services"
    },
    {
      "example": "Agency Owner: 'Plug-and-Profit Pipeline'",
      "specifics": "One offer page, 20 email templates, follow-up tracker over 30 days to turn cold leads into booked calls without manual outreach.",
      "lesson": "Tangible deliverables (templates, tracker, page) make the product real and visualizable vs. abstract 'lead gen service'"
    },
    {
      "example": "Community Owner: '30-Day Sprint Blueprint'",
      "specifics": "Guided checklist, 4 live calls, progress tracking over 30 days to help members hit one specific win without creating more content. Mechanism: Focus on execution, not education.",
      "lesson": "Fixed timeline (30 days) and clear mechanism (accountability vs. content) differentiate from typical 'community access' model"
    },
    {
      "example": "SaaS: 'Inbox-to-CRM Pipeline'",
      "specifics": "Automatic data capture, email sequencing, deal tracking over 14 days to save 10+ hours per week without manual data entry. Mechanism: Watch inbox, fill CRM, send follow-ups.",
      "lesson": "Even software benefits from product-ization—specific outcome (10+ hours saved) and simple mechanism (3 steps) vs. vague 'workflow automation'"
    },
    {
      "example": "Competitor Comparison Table: Traditional Agency vs. The 90-Day System",
      "specifics": "Traditional: vague timelines, hourly billing, no clear deliverables. The System: fixed 90 days, flat fee, 10 scripts + 1 funnel + tracking, 5-10 calls/week or refund.",
      "lesson": "Advanced play—reframe the entire market by comparing traditional category to your specific product, making all competitors look commoditized"
    }
  ],

  "objections_handled": [
    {
      "objection": "How much does it cost? (asked early in call)",
      "response": "Totally fair question—before we get there, let me make sure this is even a fit. [Ask qualifying questions.] Redirect to product explanation before price discussion."
    },
    {
      "objection": "My offer is inherently the same as competitors—how can I differentiate?",
      "response": "Commoditization isn't about sameness, it's about perception. Name it, scope it, add tangible deliverables, and package it with a clear mechanism. No one else has 'The 90-Day Client Acquisition System' even if others do ad management."
    },
    {
      "objection": "I can't create a fixed timeline—every client is different",
      "response": "The timeline creates boundaries and value. Map phases (Week 1-2: Build, Week 3-6: Optimize, Week 7-12: Scale) even if execution varies. The perception of structure matters more than perfect accuracy."
